fastapi
uvicorn
# uvicorn ships NO WebSocket implementation of its own - without one it
# answers every ws:// upgrade with "Unsupported upgrade request" and the
# handshake fails. This app is ENTIRELY WS-driven (backend/app.py's /ws
# endpoint is the whole client/server contract), so a clean install
# without this is a non-functional app, not a degraded one.
#
# This was a real shipped bug, not a test-only gap: it went unnoticed
# because the pytest suite drives /ws through FastAPI's TestClient (an
# in-process ASGI transport that never performs a real HTTP upgrade), and
# every dev machine happened to have `websockets` pulled in by some
# unrelated package. ADR-015 stage 15.6's E2E job - the first thing here
# to ever run a REAL browser against a REAL uvicorn from a clean install -
# is what surfaced it.
#
# `websockets` rather than the `uvicorn[standard]` extra: standard also
# drags in httptools/uvloop/watchfiles/PyYAML/python-dotenv, none of which
# this app uses. uvicorn auto-detects whichever implementation is present.
websockets
pywebview
